            <ArticleTitle>Submucous infiltration of betamethasone and lidocaine in the treatment of vulvar vestibulitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of persistent vulvar vestibulitis treated for several years unsuccessfully that has come to an end using a six week course of submucous infiltration of betamethasone and lidocaine in the vestibular area.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
